<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Erotokritos</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">early 17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Erotokritos is a verse romance in the Cretan dialect of Greek written by Vitsentzos Kornaros in the early 17th century under Venetian rule. Its more than 10,000 rhyming fifteen-syllable lines tell of the love of Erotokritos for the princess Aretousa and his trials to win her. The greatest work of the Cretan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a>, it remained widely known and recited in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> for centuries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/erotokritos.jpg" alt="Erotokritos" width="320" height="518" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Theophilos Chatzimichael · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Erotokritos_and_Arethousa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
